1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,520
A robot wants this cup.
机器人想拿起杯子。

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,900
The handle looks clear.
杯柄看起来是空的。

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,360
Will the fingers actually fit?
手指真能穿过去吗？

4
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:08,340
DoF Infra, episode three.
DoF Infra 第三期。

5
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:11,060
This one decision takes us through three dimensional vision.
一个抓取决策，带我们理解三维视觉。

6
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,780
Keep this cup in view.
一直看着这只杯子。

7
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:15,460
Change the question, and we may need a different representation.
问题改变，需要的表示也可能改变。

8
00:00:16,023 --> 00:00:17,743
The camera sees an image.
相机得到一张图像。

9
00:00:17,743 --> 00:00:22,223
With depth, each valid pixel also records the visible surface depth.
加入深度，每个有效像素也记录可见表面的深度。

10
00:00:22,223 --> 00:00:24,743
Calibration turns that pixel and depth
标定把像素与深度

11
00:00:24,743 --> 00:00:26,403
into an X, Y, Z position.
转换成 X、Y、Z 坐标。

12
00:00:26,403 --> 00:00:29,403
Repeat this for many pixels: a point cloud.
对许多像素重复，就得到点云。

13
00:00:29,403 --> 00:00:31,143
Now walk around the cup.
现在绕到杯子后面。

14
00:00:31,143 --> 00:00:33,883
Those missing points on the back were never measured.
背面缺失的点从未被测量过。

15
00:00:33,883 --> 00:00:37,063
Moving the display camera cannot reveal new evidence.
旋转展示视角，不会产生新证据。

16
00:00:37,653 --> 00:00:41,533
Points can carry color, normals, or confidence:
点可以携带颜色、法向或置信度：

17
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:44,333
local orientation and how much to trust each sample.
局部朝向，以及每个采样有多可信。

18
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:48,233
Depth maps keep samples arranged by camera pixels.
深度图按相机像素组织采样。

19
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:50,913
Height fields store one height per ground location,
高度场每个地面位置只存一个高度，

20
00:00:50,913 --> 00:00:52,893
so overhangs need another representation.
因此悬挑结构需要其他表示。

21
00:00:53,545 --> 00:00:57,005
Give each point an oriented patch and you have surfels:
给每个点加上有朝向的小面片，就得到 Surfel：

22
00:00:57,005 --> 00:00:58,525
little pieces of surface,
局部的表面片，

23
00:00:58,525 --> 00:01:00,325
without a shared triangle network.
不必共享三角连接。

24
00:01:00,325 --> 00:01:03,045
A mesh makes connections explicit.
Mesh 显式给出连接关系。

25
00:01:03,045 --> 00:01:05,285
Vertices join through edges and faces.
顶点通过边和面连接。

26
00:01:05,285 --> 00:01:07,445
Watch what happens if we connect the wrong neighbors.
看看连错邻居会怎样。

27
00:01:07,445 --> 00:01:09,825
This triangle seals the handle.
这个三角面封住了杯柄。

28
00:01:09,825 --> 00:01:13,265
The surface looks complete, yet the opening has disappeared.
表面看似完整，开口却消失了。

29
00:01:13,265 --> 00:01:15,945
Reconstruction introduced an assumption, not a measurement.
重建引入的是假设，不是测量。

30
00:01:16,485 --> 00:01:18,585
Remove that bridge.
去掉错误连接。

31
00:01:18,585 --> 00:01:21,205
Now the same points support a different surface.
同一批点，可以支持不同的表面。

32
00:01:21,205 --> 00:01:24,945
More detail does not automatically mean more trustworthy geometry.
细节更多，不意味着几何一定更可信。

33
00:01:24,945 --> 00:01:29,545
ElasticFusion builds a dense surfel map from RGB and depth.
ElasticFusion 从 RGB 与深度构建稠密 Surfel 地图。

34
00:01:29,545 --> 00:01:31,945
Repeated observations update its surface estimate.
连续观测更新表面估计。

35
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:35,338
The gripper needs a spatial query.
夹爪需要查询空间。

36
00:01:35,338 --> 00:01:38,258
Occupancy asks whether a location is occupied.
占据表示回答：某个位置是否被占用？

37
00:01:38,258 --> 00:01:41,058
Crucially, observed free space and unknown space are different.
已观测空闲与未知空间，必须区分。

38
00:01:41,058 --> 00:01:44,858
A depth ray supports free space before its first return.
深度射线支持首个回波前的空闲空间判断。

39
00:01:44,858 --> 00:01:46,818
Behind it, the map may know nothing.
后方可能依然未知。

40
00:01:46,818 --> 00:01:49,558
Voxels divide space into cells.
体素把空间切成单元。

41
00:01:49,558 --> 00:01:52,958
They can store occupancy, distance, or features.
单元可存占据、距离或特征。

42
00:01:52,958 --> 00:01:56,978
An octree subdivides selectively, saving resolution for useful detail.
八叉树选择性细分，把分辨率留给需要的细节。

43
00:01:57,467 --> 00:02:00,287
But free or occupied is not enough.
但空闲或占用还不够。

44
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:02,407
How close is the finger to the wall?
手指离杯壁多近？

45
00:02:02,407 --> 00:02:03,947
A distance field answers that.
距离场回答这个问题。

46
00:02:03,947 --> 00:02:07,107
An SDF adds an inside or outside sign.
SDF 额外区分内部与外部。

47
00:02:07,107 --> 00:02:09,187
An unsigned distance field keeps distance
无符号距离场只保留距离，

48
00:02:09,187 --> 00:02:11,107
without requiring a global interior.
不要求定义全局内部。

49
00:02:11,107 --> 00:02:14,927
A truncated SDF fuses depth near surfaces.
TSDF 在表面附近融合深度。

50
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:18,927
For planning, an E SDF estimates Euclidean clearance to mapped obstacles.
规划使用的 ESDF，估计到已建图障碍物的欧氏间距。

51
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:22,650
Suppose we want to redesign the handle.
如果要重新设计杯柄。

52
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:25,590
CAD keeps dimensions and constraints editable;
CAD 保留可编辑的尺寸和约束；

53
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,390
NURBS describe smooth parametric curves and surfaces.
NURBS 描述光滑的参数曲线与曲面。

54
00:02:28,390 --> 00:02:32,010
Constructive solid geometry combines simple solids
构造实体几何组合简单实体，

55
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:34,970
by union, intersection, or subtraction.
通过并集、交集或差集。

56
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:37,470
Subtracting a shape can create the opening deliberately.
减去一个形状，可以有意做出开口。

57
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:41,990
For deformation, a surface alone misses the material inside.
要模拟形变，仅有表面还缺少内部材料。

58
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:44,650
Volume meshes divide that material into cells;
体网格把材料切成单元，

59
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:46,150
physics supplies how they respond.
物理模型决定它们如何响应。

60
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:48,919
Now change the question.
现在换个问题。

61
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:51,639
We want a photograph from a new camera position.
从新的相机位置生成一张照片。

62
00:02:51,639 --> 00:02:54,539
Appearance becomes the target, rather than finger clearance.
目标变成外观，而不是手指间距。

63
00:02:54,539 --> 00:02:58,219
NeRF queries density and view dependent color along rays,
NeRF 沿射线查询密度与视角相关颜色，

64
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:00,339
then integrates them into pixels.
再积分得到像素。

65
00:03:00,339 --> 00:03:02,639
The original figure shows that rendering process.
原论文这张图展示了渲染过程。

66
00:03:02,639 --> 00:03:07,319
3D Gaussian Splatting instead optimizes spatial Gaussian primitives,
3D Gaussian Splatting 优化空间中的高斯基元，

67
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:10,099
projects them, and blends their contributions into an image.
再投影并混合它们对图像的贡献。

68
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:13,650
2D Gaussian Splatting uses oriented disks
2D Gaussian Splatting 使用有朝向的圆盘，

69
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:16,030
for stronger surface consistency.
增强表面一致性。

70
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,930
Light fields describe rays.
光场描述光线。

71
00:03:17,930 --> 00:03:19,990
These choices organize appearance differently.
它们以不同方式组织外观。

72
00:03:19,990 --> 00:03:23,730
A convincing rendered view does not certify collision safety.
渲染得逼真，不能证明碰撞安全。

73
00:03:23,730 --> 00:03:25,530
The model must answer your actual question.
模型必须回答实际的问题。

74
00:03:26,198 --> 00:03:29,318
Once the hand moves, structure matters.
手动起来后，结构也很重要。

75
00:03:29,318 --> 00:03:31,118
Skeletons organize joints;
骨架组织关节；

76
00:03:31,118 --> 00:03:34,818
parametric models such as MANO connect pose and shape to a hand mesh.
MANO 等参数模型，把姿态和形状连接到手部网格。

77
00:03:34,818 --> 00:03:37,338
A scene graph can say the cup is on the table,
场景图可以表达：杯子在桌上，

78
00:03:37,338 --> 00:03:39,298
and the hand is approaching it.
手正靠近杯子。

79
00:03:39,298 --> 00:03:41,238
Relations complement metric geometry.
关系信息补充度量几何。

80
00:03:41,238 --> 00:03:44,818
Add time, and geometry or appearance can change.
加入时间，几何或外观都可能变化。

81
00:03:44,818 --> 00:03:47,018
Scene flow, tracked objects, and dynamic fields
场景流、目标跟踪与动态场，

82
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,478
encode different kinds of motion.
表达不同层面的运动。

83
00:03:49,058 --> 00:03:52,438
So this is a toolbox, not a ladder.
所以它是工具箱，不是一条升级阶梯。

84
00:03:52,438 --> 00:03:55,038
Observe with samples, connect a surface,
用采样观测，连接表面，

85
00:03:55,038 --> 00:03:57,558
query space, render appearance, and track structure.
查询空间、渲染外观、跟踪结构。

86
00:03:57,558 --> 00:04:00,758
Explicit geometry stores elements.
显式几何存储元素。

87
00:04:00,758 --> 00:04:02,798
Implicit fields answer queries.
隐式场回答查询。

88
00:04:02,798 --> 00:04:06,018
Either can be learned; neural versus analytic is a separate choice.
两者都可以学习；神经与解析是另一条划分维度。

89
00:04:06,546 --> 00:04:09,426
For our cup, preserve what was measured,
回到这只杯子：保留测量证据，

90
00:04:09,426 --> 00:04:10,666
mark what is unknown,
标清未知区域，

91
00:04:10,666 --> 00:04:13,226
and test the gripper against the geometry that matters.
用与任务相关的几何检验夹爪。

92
00:04:13,226 --> 00:04:16,806
The papers and learning map are in our GitHub project.
原论文与学习地图都在 GitHub 项目。

93
00:04:16,806 --> 00:04:18,926
Start with the question your robot needs answered.
从机器人真正需要回答的问题出发。
